WEBVTT

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:18.740
"Together with Maman"

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.080
<i>Together with Maman</i>!

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:24.630
Hello, kids! I'm Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>!
How are you?!

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:27.130
Hello!

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.130
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.470
It's time for some fun exercises!

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:33.970
Now, come gather around me!

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.970
Yep, yep! Quickly now, gather around!

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.020
Okay! This way!

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:41.600
Don't make me exert myself, okay?

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.280
Okay! Today's <i>Together</i>
<i>with Maman </i>is starting now!

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.320
Oniisan. Your voice is hoarse.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.030
I'm okay. It's just from
all my hard drinking.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:23.580
"Life Lessons with Uramichi Oniisan"

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.750
Episode 1: Uramichi-oniisan

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:30.960
Okay, kids! Who's full
of energy today again?!

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.630
Me!

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.840
Who's feeling just fine today?!

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.430
Me!

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:40.310
Who's feeling weary and having a hard day,
so you don't wanna do anything?

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.480
Me...

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:48.400
I see... Just me, huh?

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.940
I see...

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:55.240
Pow, pow, pow, pow...

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.780
Hm?

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.320
"Whop, whop, whop..."

00:02:56.110 --> 00:03:00.410
What're you doing, Yuka-<i>chan</i>?
A surprise attack?

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:04.370
I'm casting a spell to cheer you up.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:05.910
Yuka-<i>chan</i>...

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:12.760
Well then, I'll cast a very
special spell on you all, too.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:15.090
What kind of spell?

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:20.720
A spell to prevent you from becoming
someone like me in 20 years.

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:27.440
Okay, cut! We'll take a break here!

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.980
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>!

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:30.940
"Break"

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.520
"ABC Exercise"

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:38.450
All right, kids! It's time
for the ABC Exercise!

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.280
Hmm?

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.700
Well, that was the original plan.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.790
But today, we'll change
it to the Uramichi Exercise.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.410
"ABC Exercise"

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:49.710
I wrote the lyrics and composed it
with everything I had!

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:52.800
I'll figure out the
sound effects and such,

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.630
so you just kind of feel it out
and follow my lead, okay?

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:58.430
How come we're not doing the ABC Exercise?

00:03:58.430 --> 00:04:02.010
I wanna do the ABC Exercise.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.770
It's a little protest against ***RAC.

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:07.390
Since it's the company
who has to pay JAS***,

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.310
I don't have any direct involvement,
nor do I suffer any loss.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:14.020
Sometimes taking action simply
because you get ticked off

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:17.530
is important to keep
a healthy mind, even for adults.

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.620
Gather around!

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:26.040
Okay, kids! What's Uramichi's "U" for?

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.210
♪ Up, up and away to the beach! ♪

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.960
Okay, next! What's "ra" for?

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.960
♪ Rather not do anything! ♪

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.960
Good, good! Next, what's
Uramichi's "mi" for?

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.960
♪ Missing from my life! ♪

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:37.970
What's "chi" for?

00:04:37.970 --> 00:04:40.880
♪ Child-like happiness! ♪

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.430
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:47.470
Wonderful! What good kids you are!
You sure do pick things up fast!

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:51.770
You go at it with all you've got even
when you're not really interested.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:56.730
Remember that attitude, because it'll
definitely help you when job hunting.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:00.990
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>! What's job hunting?

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:07.120
It's the crossroads of your life that
you all may run into in the future.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.870
Okay...

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:14.840
You'll all certainly be shot down and
hurt in many other situations, too,

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:18.880
but always make sure
not to lose sight of who you are.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:21.800
The "good kids," who I love the most,

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:25.970
are the strong kids with a good
right hook that they keep hidden.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:33.900
Okay, cut! That's good!

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.310
See you next time!

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:38.070
Bye-bye!

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:41.610
We'll shoot another session
with different children,

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.410
so please take a break.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:44.570
Okay!

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:47.080
Uramichi-<i>kun</i>! Good work!

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.790
Thank you very much!

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.000
"Together with Maman"

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:56.090
Ah!

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.880
It's Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>!

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.920
Quick change

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:00.920
Are you going home, too?

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.590
I'm taking a break right now.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.510
Why?

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.260
Room 7

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:08.180
Just like you kids can't play anymore
when you become sleepy,

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:12.850
my facial muscles will die
unless I give them a break.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.310
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>!

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:24.660
Okay! Today's <i>Together</i>
<i>with Maman </i>is starting now!

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:26.450
Actually, before that...

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:30.040
It looks like Miki-<i>chan</i>
has a question for me!

