Omota-sama

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:45.130
What?

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:48.880
Like I said, come out when
we call you the second time.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:53.260
But... the script says when
you call us the third time.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:56.600
The script or my throat.
Which one is more important?

00:08:56.600 --> 00:09:00.560
Uramichi Omota. 31 years old. Single.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.230
He's a gymnast <i>oniisan</i>.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:08.190
He graduated from a physical education
college and is a former gymnast.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.610
So, his body trunk is stable.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:14.200
But he's emotionally unstable.

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.910
Recently, whenever I speak loudly,

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.040
something gets taken away from me.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:23.500
What does?

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.040
My spirit.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:31.050
I wonder why he's in this profession.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:35.510
Uramichi-<i>san</i>. You were
an elite at our college,

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:38.850
and as your <i>kohai</i>, we admire you.

00:09:38.850 --> 00:09:42.390
Remember? That professor said...

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.810
...that the game is over
the moment you give up.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:53.780
There are games you're not allowed
to quit even when you give up.

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.780
Like... let's say... life.

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:03.670
Today's shooting is a wrap.
Thank you for your hard work.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:06.340
Is Uramichi-<i>kun </i>coming
to the drinking party today?

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:08.670
He's already gone home.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:12.090
What?! That was fast as always.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:13.840
Shibuya City
Smoking Rules

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:24.190
Any adult would be two-faced
or even three-faced.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:34.490
You kids pretend that you
didn't see anything, okay?

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:40.660
Wednesday

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:51.210
Ugh... morning has come again...

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:58.850
All right, then! It's time
for the ABC Exercise!

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:01.680
Did you stop fighting JAS***?

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.980
It wasn't a fight.
It was a rash act of protest.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:09.650
Flip-flopping on their positions from
day-to-day... is a habit of weak adults.

00:11:09.650 --> 00:11:11.110
Okay...

00:11:11.110 --> 00:11:14.110
Okay, then! Kids! Come gather around!

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:16.070
Oniisan, is that your natural voice?

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:19.830
You think I might be deliberately
forcing out an extra cheerful voice?

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:22.330
That's not the case at all!

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.410
This isn't where you should laugh!

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:27.370
Hey, Oniisan. Did something good
happen to you recently?

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:29.380
No, nothing!

00:11:29.380 --> 00:11:30.960
Don't laugh here, either!

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.300
Why are you smiling when
nothing good happened?

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:38.010
It's precisely because nothing
good happens, I need to at least smile.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:39.050
Er...

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:43.180
That being said, when I'm at home,
I'm alone and my feelings become numb.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:48.690
So, when I play with you kids,
I feel the most alive.

00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:51.440
This is where you should laugh.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:56.610
I don't think being alone is bad
or makes me a loser at all.

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.820
Also, I see middle-aged guys at bars
who've weirdly come to terms with life,

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:03.370
thinking they're the happiest ones even
though they're single all their lives.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:06.870
In short, regardless of if you're with
four other people or with just one person,

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:10.830
once you feel sad,
I think that makes you a loser.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:14.710
You try to apply a compress
on your back and mess it up,

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:19.010
or you blankly stare
at the walls or floor...

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:21.970
That means the solitude
has already beaten you.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.260
What about you, Oniisan?

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.720
Hm?

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:29.900
I'm crushed every day...
to the point where it's overkill.

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:31.770
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>...

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:37.950
Okay, kids! Let's call out to our friends,
Usao-<i>kun </i>and Kumao-<i>kun</i>!

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:39.450
One, two...

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:42.620
What do we do? Go out sooner?

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:41.450
Usao-<i>kun</i>!

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:46.830
Kumao-<i>kun</i>!

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:46.830
If we wait too long, Uramichi-<i>san</i>
will get upset again, right?

00:12:46.830 --> 00:12:51.500
I'm a pro, too! I'll choose to follow
the script rather than a scary <i>senpai</i>!

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:52.960
Usahara...

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.250
Smile

00:12:57.010 --> 00:13:00.260
We'll be out!
We'll be right out! I'm sorry!

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:05.640
Kids! Usao-<i>kun </i>and Kumao-<i>kun</i>
said they want to play with you.

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:06.890
Is that okay?

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:08.560
Yeah!

00:13:08.560 --> 00:13:14.980
Wow! It's a good thing that they're nice!
Right, Usao-<i>kun</i>? Kumao-<i>kun</i>?

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:17.440
What would you like to do, Usao-<i>kun</i>?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.740
Well...

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:23.160
I want to do something fun, hop!

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:27.290
I feel the same way.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:30.500
Then let's play tag!
You're good at it, right?

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:34.000
You kids chase him around
with no mercy, okay?

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.170
Okay!

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.500
I'm looking forward to it, hop!

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:41.180
You'll do something funny for the
number of times you get caught, right?

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:43.430
Now, kids! Go chase him!

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:45.550
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:48.140
Thank you for your hard work!

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:49.640
Uramichi...

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:50.480
Uramichi...

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:51.940
...-<i>san</i>!

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:54.690
Please stop tormenting me
just because I'm your <i>kohai</i>!

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:56.520
It's a form of communication.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:59.530
Your method of communication
is too messed up!

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:03.160
But, Usahara. You always say
that you wanna become funny.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.740
I've never said that!

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:06.370
I thought I'd train you.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:08.160
Like I said, I didn't say that!

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:13.210
When you're drunk, you always say that
you wanna be funny and popular with girls.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:15.830
He's lying, right?

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:17.210
I've heard it at least 100 times.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:18.500
No way...

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.550
By the way, take off your costume.
It's hot inside, isn't it?

00:14:21.550 --> 00:14:23.340
What? Oh, um...

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:26.390
He said he didn't wanna see you face
to face without getting drunk first

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:28.930
because your eyes are... scary.

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:32.270
Don't betray me like that without even
a second thought! Give me a break!

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:34.690
We were never in
collusion in the first place.

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:38.520
You don't take off the costume
for the same reason!

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.900
Ahh! Of all the things,
his straight face is the scariest!

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:46.690
"Mud Boat"
"Izakaya"
"Beer"

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:50.120
So... Uramichi-<i>san</i>...

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:52.790
What should I do?

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:55.170
What should I do?!

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.840
Tobikichi Usahara, 28 years old.

00:14:57.840 --> 00:15:00.380
Graduated from a physical education
college and is Uramichi's <i>kohai</i>.

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:02.380
This is the guy inside Usao.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:07.430
He's always broke, and his idea of
"saving" is putting money in a piggy bank.

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:09.350
What should I...

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.850
Excuse me! Two hot saké, please!

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:17.230
Mitsuo Kumatani, 28 years old.

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:22.440
Same as Usahara,
he's also Uramichi's <i>kohai</i>.

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:25.610
who doesn't make use of his
broader perspective at all.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:28.120
He's the one inside Kumao.

00:15:28.120 --> 00:15:30.330
And two saké cups as well.

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:33.910
I wanna be funny and popular with girls.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.710
Should we get water for him?

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:38.000
A glass of water, too, please!

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.960
"Together with Maman"

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:47.380
Thanks for joining us today!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.470
See you next time, kids!

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:54.350
I hope you'll watch
<i>Together with Maman </i>again!

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:56.020
Bye-bye!

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:58.060
Bye-bye!

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:00.110
Okay, cut!

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:03.530
That's good! Thank you for your hard work!

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.820
Iketeru Daga, 27 years old.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.740
He's a singer <i>oniisan</i>.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.990
He used to be a musical actor

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:18.290
and is a very talented singer
with a strong, deep, and pretty voice.

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:21.460
Although he's blessed with good looks,

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:26.550
he loves crass, dirty humor and can't read
between the lines or sense the mood.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:31.600
What time is it now?

00:16:31.600 --> 00:16:33.810
What do you have that watch for?

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:37.430
In addition, he has a hard time
telling time from an analog watch.

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:42.270
Utano Tadano, 32 years old.

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:44.230
She's a singer <i>oneesan</i>.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:48.200
Her unique experience after graduating
from a famous music college includes

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:51.780
being an unpopular pop star,
an <i>enka </i>singer, an impressionist,

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:54.910
a jazz singer in a nightclub,
and now a singer <i>oneesan</i>.

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.660
Just got married

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.660
Just got married

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:04.750
By the way, it's been over
five years since she started living

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:07.340
with her unpopular comedian boyfriend.

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:08.970
I wanna get married.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:12.890
Are you listening?

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:16.810
What? Oh, sorry. I was
thinking about something.

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:20.890
Okay, cut!

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:24.190
Thank you for your hard work!

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.980
We'll set up for the second session,
so please take a break now.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.190
Okay!

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:31.410
Seriously, Uramichi-<i>san </i>is--

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:42.580
I'm so out of it that I don't even care
about the annoying guy who appears

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.920
to be acutely aware of my presence.

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:48.590
This is a terminal symptom.
I'm starting to feel very sad.

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.590
What? He ignored me?

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.430
That's even scarier.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:54.970
"Green Room
for Uramichi Omota-<i>sama</i>"

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:05.860
I think people start growing old
once they stop fighting.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:09.940
Even if it's not an aggressive thing
like fighting instinct,

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:13.110
you unconsciously fight, compete,
experience hardships, and get crushed.

00:18:13.110 --> 00:18:16.780
That's how you grow as a human being.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:20.500
That bunny kind of took
a quick glance at me earlier.

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:24.460
He was probably about to say
bad things about me.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:27.960
When he checked to see if I was there,
just in case, we made firm eye contact.

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:31.590
So, he was like, "Oh crap!"
and "He's right there."

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:34.930
But that's just the norm,
so I don't really care in this case.

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:41.980
What's scary is my emotional ups and
downs started lagging a little behind.

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:50.570
Things that happen and the emotions
that I should feel about them...

00:18:50.570 --> 00:18:54.070
I feel like they aren't quite linked.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:58.910
The feeling that the "anger"
is changing into "indifference"...

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.160
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>...

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:04.750
Iketeru-<i>oniisan</i>! You should knock, okay?

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:06.830
So, what brings you here?

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:10.420
Do you know about the
physicist Richard Feynman?

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.340
Er...

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:14.760
Yeah. I've heard of him.

00:19:14.760 --> 00:19:17.640
He studied particles or whatever, right?

00:19:21.270 --> 00:19:26.190
I learned about him just earlier.
I laughed so hard

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:29.060
that I almost couldn't breathe...

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:32.650
‘Cause his nickname... would be "Dick."

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:35.490
Don't you think it's really funny?

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:38.570
Dick... Dick Feynman, you know?

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:42.290
There you are! Both of you,
please get ready!

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:49.960
Richard Feynman.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:50.500
Di--

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.880
Ding-a-Ling.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:56.220
Hm? Is something wrong?

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:58.510
No, I'm okay.

00:19:58.510 --> 00:19:59.890
Giggle stick.

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:05.430
Please... stop it already!
The shooting starts soon.

00:20:05.430 --> 00:20:08.310
Pocket rocket.

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:10.690
Pocket rocket... Pocket rocket...

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:13.690
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>.

00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:17.150
Okay, then! We'll start shooting
the second session now!

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:17.230
"Together with Maman"

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:22.120
Hello, kids! How are you?!

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:25.160
It's drawing fun time!

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:27.660
Let me and Uramichi-<i>oniisan </i>play with you

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:30.080
until Iketeru-<i>oniisan</i>
is in good condition.

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:32.960
Is Iketeru-<i>oniisan </i>not in good condition?

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:38.130
No, he's not. I'd actually say
he's already a little broken.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:41.220
You kids make sure that you
take breaks when you work hard

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:43.310
so that you can avoid going crazy

00:20:43.310 --> 00:20:46.350
from exhaustion, which can
eat away at your mind.

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.230
What about Iketeru-<i>oniisan</i>?

00:20:48.230 --> 00:20:50.190
It's too late for him.

00:20:50.190 --> 00:20:51.940
I feel sorry for him.

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:57.240
More importantly, Utano-<i>oneesan</i>,
what are we going to draw today?

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:01.160
Today... let's draw our friends!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:05.870
First, Uramichi-<i>oniisan </i>will draw
his friend and show it to you!

00:21:05.870 --> 00:21:07.200
I'll do it just for you!

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.960
Wow...!

00:21:15.460 --> 00:21:16.590
Done!

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:18.090
What the heck is this?

00:21:18.090 --> 00:21:21.390
Wha...? Huh? What the heck... is this?

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:28.770
This is a little birdy who appears in
my dream about 80 percent of the time!

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:30.230
He's cute, isn't he?

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:32.440
Are you sick?

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:36.440
If I admit that I'm sick,
a guy like him with dangerous eyes

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:39.900
would use that to take advantage of me.

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:42.200
What are you talking about?

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:45.410
Uramichi-<i>oniisan</i>?

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:50.660
Okay, cut! Today's shooting is a wrap!

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:52.370
Thank you for your hard work!

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:58.210
Well, seriously, Uramichi-<i>san </i>has...

00:21:58.210 --> 00:21:59.050
Hm?

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:02.720
...no other hobbies besides
buffing up his body, right?

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:06.010
There's something
I wanna say to him someday.

00:22:08.390 --> 00:22:10.770
A man who loves nothing else but muscle...

00:22:10.770 --> 00:22:13.810
His name is Gloomy Macho...

00:22:14.810 --> 00:22:15.940
...cho...?

00:22:17.230 --> 00:22:21.990
That was the moment "indifference"
turned into "anger"!
